ay mix until the polls close.", "Party is registration, not the vote. Who votes on the day also depends on how many voted early or by mail."], "means": {"side": "in line", "gap_now": 7.3, "gap_proj": 9.4, "ed_left_assumed": 997573, "range": [4.2, 13.7], "ours": 5.55, "need": -3.9, "near_year": 2018, "red_from": 11.1, "names": {"R": "Moody", "D": "Nixon"}, "method": ["Every vote so far (mail, early and today) is R+7.3 by registration: Republicans minus Democrats. If Election Day ends as big as 2022's, the electorate lands near R+9.4. The final gap was R+5.3 in 2018, R+12.1 in 2022, R+11.1 in 2024.", "How far each Senate result ran from that gap, which is how independents and crossover voters broke: 5.2 points bluer in 2018, 4.3 points redder in 2022, 1.7 points redder in 2024. The same this year gives R+4.2 to R+13.7."], "race_id": "senate_fl", "ours_source": "data/daily/2026-11-01.json core[senate_fl].margin (the core model on the closing day)", "past": [{"year": 2018, "race": "Senate (Scott over Nelson)", "margin": 0.12, "gap": 5.3, "ran": -5.2, "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2018_United_States_Senate_election_in_Florida", "retrieved_at": "2026-11-03T13:27:47-05:00"}, {"year": 2022, "race": "Senate (Rubio over Demings)", "margin": 16.41, "gap": 12.1, "ran": 4.3, "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_United_States_Senate_election_in_Florida", "retrieved_at": "2026-11-03T13:26:18-05:00"}, {"year": 2024, "race": "Senate (Scott over Mucarsel-Powell)", "margin": 12.78, "gap": 11.1, "ran": 1.7, "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Florida", "retrieved_at": "2026-11-03T13:26:19-05:00"}], "lines": ["Florida's turnout so far points to a Moody win in the Senate race, by somewhere around 4 to 14 points.", "We forecast Moody by 5.6, near the Democratic end of that.", "For our number to be right, independents and crossover voters have to lean Democratic this time, about as much as in 2018. If they vote like they did in 2022 and 2024, Moody wins by 11 or more, about 6 points redder than we expect.", "What to watch tonight: Florida's count landing near Moody by 6 means our forecast is holding. Moody by 11 or more means the night is running redder than we expected.", "Based on three past elections, and registration is not how people vote. A lean, not a call. It firms up as Election Day votes come in."], "label": "inferred", "how": "Registration gap = GOP share minus DEM share of the people voting. The range adds each year's gap between the Senate result and the registration gap to this year's projected gap. Scripts do the arithmetic (scripts/night_batches.py reading)."}, "label": "inferred", "how": "Shares of the people voting, by registration. 'Looks like' a year means the GOP-minus-DEM share gap is within 2 points of that year's whole Election Day."}, "feed": {"tried_at": "2026-11-03T14:33:20-05:00", "source": "Fresh Take Florida (freshtake.vote), the sum of its 67 county rows", "url": "https://www.freshtake.vote/2026G/", "every_minutes": 10, "ok_at": "2026-11-03T14:33:20-05:00", "updated": "2026-11-03T14:32:09-05:00", "counties": 67, "counties_eday": 67, "ok": true, "result": "saved B048: 1,608,125 Election Day votes as of 2:32pm", "saved": "B048"}}}, "order": ["FL"], "how": "Each report is the running count of today's voters by registration. A batch is the change from the report before. Scripts do the arithmetic (scripts/night_batches.py)."}